---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base title="TinyCompiler" description="One tiny tensor program, compiled to two real chips and checked bit-exact.">
  <main>
    <header style="margin: 24px 0 8px">
      <h1 style="font-size: 28px">One tensor program. Two real chips. Bit-exact.</h1>
      <p style="font-size: 17px; max-width: 720px">
        TinyCompiler turns <code>C = relu(A @ B)</code> into
        <a href="https://github.com/deaneeth/tiny-gpu">tiny-gpu</a> SIMT kernels and into a
        <a href="https://github.com/deaneeth/tiny-tpu">tiny-tpu</a> tile schedule. Both run on the real
        simulator and the real RTL, and both match numpy exactly.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/app"><button class="primary">Open the Compiler Explorer</button></a> <a href="/docs/" style="margin-left: 12px">Read the docs</a></p>
    </header>

    <section class="panel" style="margin: 20px 0">
      <h2 style="font-size: 17px; margin-top: 0">What is checked, on every commit</h2>
      <ul style="margin: 0; padding-left: 18px">
        <li>Every result equals a numpy oracle computed from the <em>source</em> program, on both chips.</li>
        <li>Differential fuzzing: random programs through every backend and optimization level on the real chips; 5,000-program runs were green twice.</li>
        <li>The chips' facts the compiler relies on are measured and pinned (tiny-tpu: 15 cycles per pass; tiny-gpu: a loop of K iterations costs K cycles).</li>
        <li>The TPU cost model equals the measured RTL cycles exactly.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section class="panel" style="margin: 20px 0">
      <h2 style="font-size: 17px; margin-top: 0">Optimizing the tiny-gpu kernel (8×8 matmul + relu, measured)</h2>
      <table>
        <thead><tr><th>level</th><th>instructions</th><th>cycles</th><th>global loads</th></tr></thead>
        <tbody>
          <tr><td>-O0 naive</td><td>7320</td><td>10</td><td>1088</td></tr>
          <tr><td>-O1 licm + strength reduction</td><td>5208 (−29%)</td><td>9</td><td>1024</td></tr>
          <tr><td>-O2 tiling, unrolling, folding</td><td>3288 (−55%)</td><td>3</td><td>576 (−47%)</td></tr>
        </tbody>
      </table>
      <p class="muted" style="margin-bottom: 0">
        Per-pass numbers, and why -O2 is not simply better, are in <a href="/docs/architecture">the architecture notes</a>.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="muted">
      TinyCompiler is the fourth project in a series with
      <a href="https://github.com/deaneeth/tiny-gpu">tiny-gpu</a>,
      <a href="https://github.com/deaneeth/tiny-tpu">tiny-tpu</a> and tiny-cpu.
    </p>
  </main>
</Base>
